**Commentary of al-Shinqiti (Adwa' al-Bayan) on surah 21, verse 32:**

His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿And We made the sky a protected ceiling, yet they turn away from its signs.﴾

This noble verse includes three matters:

The first: Allah, majestic and exalted, made the sky a ceiling, meaning that it is for the earth as a ceiling is for a house.

The second: He made that ceiling protected.

(p-144) The third: the disbelievers turn away from the signs in it, that is, the sky, and do not take admonition from it or remember. He has clarified these three matters in other places.

As for His making it a ceiling, He mentioned in surah "al-Tur" that it is raised, in His saying: ﴿By the mount [al-Tur], and a Book inscribed, in parchment unrolled, and the frequented House, and the raised ceiling [al-Saqf al-Marfu']﴾ [al-Tur: - 5].

As for that ceiling being protected, He clarified it in various places of His Book. He made clear that it is protected from falling, in His saying: ﴿And He holds the sky from falling upon the earth except by His permission﴾ [al-Hajj: 65];

and His saying: ﴿And of His signs is that the sky and the earth stand by His command﴾ [al-Rum: 25];

and His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿Indeed, Allah holds the heavens and the earth lest they cease﴾ [Fatir: 41];

and His saying: ﴿His Kursi extends over the heavens and the earth, and their preservation does not tire Him, and He is the Most High, the Most Great﴾ [al-Baqarah: 255];

and His saying: ﴿And We have certainly created above you seven paths, and We have not been unaware of creation﴾ [al-Mu'minun: 17], according to the view of those who say: "and We have not been unaware of creation," for if We were to be heedless, the sky would fall upon them and destroy them. He also made clear that it is protected from cracking and splitting, and that it does not need repair or restoration as other ceilings do when their time lengthens,

such as His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿Then return your gaze; do you see any breaks?﴾ [al-Mulk: 3];

and His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿Have they not looked at the sky above them, how We constructed it and adorned it, and it has no flaws?﴾ [Qaf: 6], meaning: there are in it no cracks or fissures. He also made clear that the aforementioned ceiling is protected from every accursed devil,

such as His saying: ﴿And We have protected it from every accursed devil﴾ [al-Hijr: 17]. We have explained the verses indicating its protection from all the devils in surah "al-Hijr."

As for the disbelievers turning away from the signs in it, He clarified this in various places of His Book,

such as His saying, may He be exalted: ﴿And how many a sign in the heavens and the earth they pass by, while turning away from it﴾ [Yusuf: 105];

and His saying: ﴿And if they see a sign, they turn away﴾ [al-Qamar: 2], the verse;

and His saying: ﴿Indeed, those upon whom the word of your Lord has been fulfilled will not believe, even if every sign should come to them﴾ [Yunus: 96–97];

and His saying: ﴿And the signs and warnings do not avail a people who do not believe﴾ [Yunus: 101].
